# Environment for the /devnet deployment ("staging-devnet") and local devnet runs.
#
# Loaded by `npm run build:devnet`, which sources this file before running
# `next build` with BASE_PATH=/devnet. Next.js does not auto-load `.env.devnet`,
# so the values below only take effect through that script. The same file is read
# by scripts/sdk-env.mjs, so `NETWORK=devnet node scripts/<script>.mjs` picks up
# the same wiring without repeating it on the command line.
#
# This file is checked in on purpose: contract IDs, identity IDs and node
# addresses are public data. Never put a seed phrase, WIF, or any other private
# key material here — those live in `.env.local` (gitignored) or GitHub secrets.
#
# SAKURA (Platform 5.0.0-beta.3, protocol 14, node network id
# dash-devnet-sakura; docs/PLATFORM_V5_BETA3_UPGRADE.md). Sakura's PLATFORM
# chain was wiped again for 5.0.0-beta.3 on 2026-10-08 (Core was kept), so
# every earlier sakura id in git history (2026-10-01, 2026-10-06/07) is dead,
# as are all bonsia and moutai ids. Every identity was re-created from a new
# asset lock with the SAME keys (new ids), and every contract below is new
# (docs/SAKURA_BETA3_DEPLOY.md).

NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK=devnet
# The SDK's devnetName is the node's network id suffix: plain `sakura`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEVNET_NAME=sakura

# All 13 validators, listed explicitly (seed-1..3.sakura… all resolve to one
# host). Each serves a Let's Encrypt IP-SAN certificate on :1443 (the current
# set expires 2026-10-11 and auto-renews).
NEXT_PUBLIC_DAPI_ADDRESSES=https://68.67.122.86:1443,https://68.67.122.87:1443,https://68.67.122.240:1443,https://68.67.122.241:1443,https://68.67.122.88:1443,https://68.67.122.89:1443,https://68.67.122.90:1443,https://68.67.122.91:1443,https://68.67.122.92:1443,https://68.67.122.93:1443,https://68.67.122.94:1443,https://68.67.122.95:1443,https://68.67.122.232:1443

# Quorum service for the trusted context (BLS public keys that verify read
# proofs). The SDK's name-derived default (quorums.sakura…) is the same host;
# it is set explicitly anyway.
NEXT_PUBLIC_QUORUM_URL=https://quorums.sakura.networks.dash.org

# Insight reports "network":"testnet" — devnets reuse testnet address and WIF
# prefixes, which is why key derivation stays on testnet (see keyNetwork()).
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSIGHT_API_URL=https://insight.sakura.networks.dash.org/insight-api

# Contracts on sakura. The maker (a new identity after the 2026-10-08 wipe, so
# contract ids are generateId(maker, nonce)) published the whole /devnet set at
# nonces 1-11 on 2026-10-08 with one publisher. All eleven are maker-owned and
# enrolled in ONE contract group, Cxxdiq5bBMFr2j8H1ug4hKaDqv7CcVYMt8PPvopj2rDF
# (DEVNET_CONTRACT_GROUP_ID below), registered by the first create (key backup,
# nonce 1) so the unchanged contracts could go first while social v14 and
# pollr v6 were in review; the rest joined it. Sources, sha256-pinned: social v14
# (b18f7c82…, docs/SOCIAL_V14.md), pollr v6 (fa081adf…), the blocks contract
# (45f04cba…), blog v7 (a04df915…) and storefront v6 (c6c9c678…,
# docs/NON_SOCIAL_CONTRACTS.md); DM v4/v5 from contracts/; key backup, key
# exchange, vault and auth vault from the testnet snapshot.
#
#   nonce 1  key backup (group)    nonce 7  storefront v6
#   nonce 2  key exchange          nonce 8  DM v4
#   nonce 3  vault                 nonce 9  DM v5
#   nonce 4  auth vault            nonce 10 social v14
#   nonce 5  blocks                nonce 11 pollr v6
#   nonce 6  blog v7
#
# Social v14 (docs/SOCIAL_V14.md) is v13 re-cut for beta.3: countPresent rules,
# a report a moderator resolved can no longer be withdrawn (deleteConstraints,
# 40147), replies store no owners (derived rootOwnerRecent/parentOwnerRecent
# windows), and an UNPAUSED YAPP. ELECTED moderation with the mainnet windows
# (7-day join, 3-day vote, a contestable seat with a 30-day cool-down), owner
# interim, ownerProtected. Until a team is seated the maker moderates as the
# interim owner. Election E1 (submitted charter
# BWnb37rYd4AhLRgXr9gnmDKoWn9z27CFDvDuazGMwFzR, contender doc
# GN7SWmrWh5a56uez7mSrGG7mWNXWcX9m2HFVWez2szRf) applied 2026-10-08 18:54Z with
# tess1999 leading alice7 and battery bot 1, both elected through join
# requests; uncontested, it seats about 2026-10-15 18:54Z. There is NO profile
# contract: the base profile is DashPay's `profile` (system contract
# Bwr4WHCPz5rFVAD87RqTs3izo4zpzwsEdKPWUT1NS1C7) and the social `yapprProfile`
# type is the extension.
#
# YAPP (social token position 0) is AMrtbchVQGGhgJR5CrGyn8qFZdfPoY3C4CqweA7qM9Jw.
# It starts UNPAUSED and can never be paused or priced: it pays post, reply and
# like token costs again under beta.3 and is transferable (Yappr offers no
# transfer UI), while direct purchases are refused (40721). Identities claim
# the 100-YAPP once-per-identity grant; the maker mints anything beyond it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_CONTRACT_ID=6GrRBNDe7r5JXZFr9XgUETKACzvrUZjHdfgKCYCMcc9y
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTRACT_TOPOLOGY=v14
# block, blockFilter and blockFollow (contracts/yappr-blocks-contract.json):
# unmoderated, read and written here on v13 and v14.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_BLOCKS_CONTRACT_ID=2huLPRT5KsC3gmbCtQ2EdWNaP697owVNCforoxDpPnXx

# Optional feature contracts, maker-owned and in the same group as social;
# their *_TOPOLOGY gates below must match. Blank an id to turn the feature off:
# services fail closed instead of querying a missing contract. Blog v7 and
# storefront v6 elect their own moderators (the same 7-day/3-day windows; the
# maker moderates as the interim owner until a team is seated) and charge
# action fees instead of YAPP, so they no longer embed the social id.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_DM_CONTRACT_ID=8a1p5yGq5rJMpWyEm25PEnDcC3kTNWGq3t8au25vC2EX
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_STOREFRONT_CONTRACT_ID=5qh1gpJY36bkEXb4PMPJ2E1VhRxZZ796FHFGWu3oCmhk
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENCRYPTED_KEY_BACKUP_CONTRACT_ID=Abe7MfKpUysqjGTvbYBo5KAEpgxwXVHX8uxWAaAYm52C
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEY_EXCHANGE_CONTRACT_ID=AidVzHpUNSDAq8Q79EiYpnrhCpkZrv1FuYhDMkES1nZg
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_VAULT_CONTRACT_ID=FbZ45amM1dnRbxD2ZngfhzJ9Mngj1tbnp7mDVGQKSDxb
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_AUTH_VAULT_CONTRACT_ID=AfkTRtNUfAuF2CckhNE5CYEEhGsBBQGfMEBGm82wbh5g
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_BLOG_CONTRACT_ID=4F1Wi4dim7j6eWrFQ3aHWEB9az5dHcJBmdvMvpx7sx1j
# Pollr v6 is registered (nonce 11, Fq5yTk2YqJZ2wa7uESKB119nX3ea23QP2gUsLqGtEu8c)
# but this client has no v6 topology until #701 merges, so polls stay OFF here
# (blank id: no poll is read, embedded or offered in compose). The follow-up
# sets the id and NEXT_PUBLIC_POLLR_TOPOLOGY=v6.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POLLR_CONTRACT_ID=

# DM v5 (docs/DM_V5.md): unlinkable 1:1 and group messaging. Every new
# conversation goes here; the DM v4 contract above is read-only and its threads
# merge into the v5 timeline.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPPR_DM_V5_CONTRACT_ID=4PU6mxANMUXaApgkUNq7VzmftMmbk8p2fUeFoiqRS79D

# Feature topology gates, each pinned to the contract registered above.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DM_TOPOLOGY=v5
NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_TOPOLOGY=v6
NEXT_PUBLIC_BLOG_TOPOLOGY=v7
NEXT_PUBLIC_POLLR_TOPOLOGY=v5

# DPNS is a system contract and normally keeps the same id on every chain; set
# this only if the devnet registered it elsewhere.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DPNS_CONTRACT_ID=

# Maker: index 9 of the privately retained deployment seed (the same key as on
# bonsia and moutai, a new identity id on each sakura chain; nonce 11 after the
# 2026-10-08 beta.3 publish).
# The dedicated CI seed is separate and cannot control the maker.
DEVNET_CONTRACT_GROUP_ID=Cxxdiq5bBMFr2j8H1ug4hKaDqv7CcVYMt8PPvopj2rDF
DEVNET_MAKER_IDENTITY_ID=9RPq2JuMsmrTUoxQLricaT245t4bYskCj4hXWcedCagH

# The devnet social contract is owned by the devnet maker, so token moderation
# (freeze/unfreeze/destroy, mint) gates on it instead of the testnet authority
# baked into lib/constants.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YAPP_TOKEN_AUTHORITY_ID=9RPq2JuMsmrTUoxQLricaT245t4bYskCj4hXWcedCagH

# Dedicated CI bots, in derivation-index order of the E2E_DEVNET_SEED_PHRASE
# secret: index 0 is the CI identity (yappr-ci-devnet-260915), 1-8 the DM v5
# e2e bots (yappr-dm-e2e-1..8, each with the seed-derived ENCRYPTION key). Same
# keys as on bonsia, new ids after each sakura wipe. Testnet credentials are unchanged.
E2E_IDENTITY_IDS=AuPAmquzMYem3mxeyAaWnzpSyok9itGU8MP19GTKMBp9,Dj2D55V8R3eVkW72XpAcpZ6J3ExLpNBr2HiSHuZd7XQw,An7sPjdxSDn2DsCoyhZjxHSWbqKtFcK3uwSLh1mXDHqa,HdiuCv9qtfTWo7R4PNFEN9B3tFxYhP5X8Cbr38jKfq87,FxjY5SSmvJqCZ6zFSGWqATvNGp1czaoLATjkEF2k57Hz,9xkQEgWa2V9v9b6Ujb9v3uJfLwVh2SXofFNXapRE64CF,7mXLFFbjNSVWyY5m8i4R5LPHhwKW7dF8vh9gNvLpGLCG,CB6dvhWfhn61Vfw17axv3AougXnMGt3oxFw8yi9DsRoc,B6Hpa1MJ3JqzA1MS38tnhRf9pBmUp4Cvkznx89NWsWEL

NEXT_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL=debug
